    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d592">

                <pb facs="0587" n="421" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg421"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 337.11/302</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Gonzales to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-17T14:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 17, 1917, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram March 16, 6 p.m. Owner here yesterday talked with me, President and
                    commander of military forces of his district. The Government promised to send
                    more troops this morning. I received telephone from the Consular agent at
                    Caibarien saying that young Atkins at Punta Alegre alarmed fearing attack from
                    Spanish bandit; they wish marines. He reported all mills except his grinding. I
                    gave information to the Navy and informed the President. He telegraphed
                    immediately commander of military district. Owner of the place says this menace
                    is from an old Spanish bandit with ninety followers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
